blockspec — third-party corpus text

Most of this repository is original work, licensed as LICENSE describes. The
text listed below is not. The spike measures public documentation corpora,
and its committed results carry their text. That text remains under
its own upstream terms, not under LICENSE's per-directory split, and it is not
offered under CC-BY-4.0.

Where it appears

  spike/results/prereg2/export/packets/
  spike/results/prereg3/export/packets/
    Every .md file in a packet other than QUESTIONS.md is a whole corpus
    file as it stood at a commit in that corpus's history, up to and
    including the pin below: before.md and after.md, or in a merge packet
    base.md, leg-a.md, leg-c.md and after.md. Each packet's packet.json
    quotes from them. The plant packets are the exception: the harness
    generates their text (3 in prereg2, 5 in prereg3). Packets per corpus,
    the same in both exports:
      kubernetes/website  340  (k8s-en 169, k8s-l10n 171)
      github/site-policy   52
      cncf/toc             32
      rust-lang/book       31
      obsidianmd/obsidian-help  28
      commonmark/commonmark-spec  0
    The counts come from recomputing each packet's name from the nonce in
    that prereg's sealed-manifest.json and the scoring units in
    spike/results/prereg2/score/, whose export both preregs share.

  elsewhere under spike/results/
    Other result files quote shorter excerpts where they report a block, a
    quote or a target: the score units, merge-arm-candidates.jsonl and the
    cheap-arm/ reports among them. A few short obsidian-help fragments, a
    file path and a heading, are also quoted in spike/LOG.md and
    spike/PRE-REGISTRATION.md.

Each corpus was read at a pinned commit. Prereg 2 and prereg 3 use the pins
in spike/PRE-REGISTRATION-2.md section 6.2 (prereg 3 keeps prereg 2's
corpora, PRE-REGISTRATION-3.md section 1). The earlier arms use
spike/harness/corpora.json (spike/LOG.md section 1) for rust-lang/book,
obsidianmd/obsidian-help and commonmark/commonmark-spec, and
spike/PRE-REGISTRATION.md section 5.1 for the other three. Where an earlier
pin differs from section 6.2, both are listed. The licence stated for each
is what the repository's tree holds at that pin.

The files themselves come from the history sampled up to the pin, and some
of that history is older than the licence the pin carries. Counted over
every commit the instances in spike/results/prereg2/score/ read files at
(the commit, its parent, both ends of a sampled span, and a merge with its
base and legs), by what each commit's own tree holds:

  rust-lang/book      474 of 1985 commits have no licence or copyright file
                      in their tree. LICENSE-APACHE and LICENSE-MIT were
                      added in 6063c71 (2017-02-12); the 474 are dated
                      2015-12-11 to 2017-03-03, the later ones on branches
                      that did not yet contain it.
  github/site-policy  9 of 255 commits predate the CC0 dedication: 8 carry
                      LICENSE.md as the CC-BY-4.0 legal code, and 1
                      (7249f63) has no LICENSE.md. 88dc965 (2017-07-11)
                      changed LICENSE.md from CC-BY-4.0 to CC0-1.0.
  kubernetes/website  unaffected: all 9064 commits carry LICENSE as the
                      CC-BY-4.0 legal code.


