Neither cncf/toc's tree nor obsidianmd/obsidian-help's carries a licence
file at its pin. Their excerpts and files are included only so the spike's
results can be reproduced and checked. All rights in them remain with their
authors, and nothing in this repository licenses them to anyone.

For cncf/toc, the CNCF charter, section 11(b)(iv), says documentation is
received and made available by the CNCF under CC-BY-4.0
(https://github.com/cncf/foundation/blob/47613dd4aeee9861644b91382aee7dcecb334afb/charter.md).
Whether that clause covers the TOC's own documents is not settled here.
